The '''2026 Islington London Borough Council election''' took place on 7 May 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-01-01 |title=Local elections in London will test support for Reform UK and Greens |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c99k0mzj7x8o |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> All 51 members of [[Islington London Borough Council]] were elected. The elections took place alongside [[2026 London local elections|local elections in the other London boroughs]] and [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|elections to local authorities across the United Kingdom]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Number of councils that have requested delay to local elections revealed - is yours one of them? |url=https://news.sky.com/story/local-elections-2026-over-a-third-of-councils-offered-a-delay-have-requested-one-is-yours-on-the-list-13494762 |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=Sky News |language=en}}</ref>

== Background ==
{{See also|Islington London Borough Council elections}}
Labour held control of the council in [[2022 Islington London Borough Council election|2022]]. In 2026, councillor [[Sara Hyde, Baroness Hyde of Bemerton|Sara Hyde]] was appointed to the [[House of Lords]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Political Peerages December 2025 |url=https://www.gov.uk/government/news/political-peerages-december-2025 |access-date=2025-12-10 |website=GOV.UK |language=en}}</ref>

